From b096ebb4fdc6db60444580e2cf158ccac7686da9
Subject: bevy_winit: synthesize key events for modifier transitions reported via ModifiersChanged
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/b096ebb4fdc6db60444580e2cf158ccac7686da9
Date: 2026-07-02T11:37:24+01:00

OS-consumed shortcut chords (e.g. macOS Cmd+Shift+5) deliver the modifier
keydowns but swallow the keyups without any focus transition, so the modifier
stays stuck in ButtonInput<KeyCode> forever — on the web there is no signal at
all to recover from. Winit re-derives modifier state from every keyboard/
pointer/wheel event and reports it via WindowEvent::ModifiersChanged, which
was previously dropped on the floor.

Buffer the latest Modifiers per window and reconcile against
WinitWindowPressedKeys at end-of-batch, before forwarding events — after the
batch's real key events have landed in the map, so normal modifier presses
synthesize nothing. Transitions that never arrived as key events (missed
keyups during OS chords, missed keydowns when focus returns with a modifier
already held) are synthesized as KeyboardInput press/release, flowing through
the same path as the existing KeyboardFocusLost machinery. Sides are resolved
via ModifiersKeyState where the platform reports them, defaulting to the left
variant (the web backend can't distinguish).
